---
description: Operational basics — interpreter, path contract, contract versions, typed scoring
alwaysApply: true
---

- Interpreter: `C:\Users\murrn\miniconda3\python.exe`. Never `.venv` (lacks the
  scientific stack).
- Outputs live on Dropbox, not in the repo: every artifact path resolves through
  `src/survey_features/layout.py` helpers under `SURVEY_FEATURES_OUTPUTS` (gitignored
  `.env`). NEVER hard-code an absolute or machine-local path in a tracked file; never
  write artifacts into the repo tree.
- Oracle contract v4 is current; v3 is a deprecated development byproduct. Do not
  build on v3-era artifacts; check `contract_version` in a cell's `oracle_meta.json`
  before trusting a cached number.
- No untyped scoring anywhere: ordinal/continuous targets are scored by Spearman rank
  correlation (regression path), never as multiclass accuracy. Always pass
  `target_type` to `survey_features.evaluation.evaluate_feature_set`.
- Where to write runs/experiments and when to register them: `CONTRIBUTING.md`.
  Repo + outputs map: `docs/project_layout.md`. Terms: `docs/glossary.md`.
